.TH FONT 2
.SH NAME
font_init,
font_get,
font_for \- the baked console font
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B import "vsys:libfont"
.PP
.nf
.B "FONT_WIDTH :: 8"
.B "FONT_HEIGHT :: 16"
.B "FONT_FIRST :: 0x20"
.B "FONT_LAST :: 0x7E"
.B "font_8x16: [FONT_LAST - FONT_FIRST + 1][FONT_HEIGHT]u8"
.fi
.PP
.B import "vsys:libmui"
.PP
.nf
.B "font_init :: proc(f: ^Fonts, first_id: u32 = 1)"
.B "font_get :: proc(f: ^Fonts, ink: libpal.RGB, bg: libpal.RGB) -> (libdraw.Atlas, bool)"
.B "font_for :: proc(f: ^Fonts, ink: libpal.RGB, bg: libpal.RGB, scratch: []u8, sink: Sink) -> (libdraw.Atlas, bool)"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Libfont
is Vectra's one console font: 8 by 16 pixel cells, one bit per pixel,
covering the printable 7-bit range,
.B FONT_FIRST
.RI ( 0x20 ,
space) through
.B FONT_LAST
.RI ( 0x7E ,
tilde).
.B Font_8x16
holds a cell per character, indexed by
.RI "character\ \-\ " FONT_FIRST ,
sixteen bytes each, one byte per scanline with the most significant bit
leftmost.
The table is generated by
.IR genfont (8)
from a host font and is not meant to be edited by hand.
A caller that draws text reads the table directly: neither
.I window
nor
.I terminal
(see
.IR window (1))
goes through any other library to put glyphs on the glass.
.PP
Every image the draw protocol (see
.IR draw (2))
accepts carries its own pixels, and a blit is opaque, so a label drawn
in one pair of ink and background colours needs a glyph image baked in
that ink over that background.
.IR Libmui 's
font package bakes one such atlas per pair, on demand, out of
.IR libfont 's
table.
.PP
A
.B Fonts
holds the atlases a window has baked and the next free image id.
.I Font_init
resets
.I f
and sets the first id it will hand out; a window that shares the
server's image pool with its own frame starts numbering past them.
.PP
.I Font_get
answers the atlas already baked for the pair
.RI ( ink ,
.IR bg ),
or
.B false
if none has been.
.I Font_for
answers that atlas too, baking and uploading it through
.I sink
first if this is the first time the pair is asked for.
.I Scratch
is one wire slot the upload commands are built in.
It answers
.B false
when the atlas pool
.RB ( MAX_FACES ,
eight pairs) is full or a write to
.I sink
failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B sys/libfont/font_data.odin
.br
.B sys/libmui/fonts.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR genfont (8),
.IR draw (2),
.IR mui (2),
.IR palette (2)
.SH BUGS
There is no font but this one, and no way to load another.
A window may bake at most eight distinct ink and background pairs; a
ninth is refused rather than evicting one already baked.
